# What the image build does not read (spec 020 #8). The context is the Go
# sources, the interface's sources, go.mod/go.sum, the Makefile and the licence
# files; everything else is upload time the daemon spends for nothing.

.git
.github/
bin/
dist/

# The interface is built inside the image from its own sources. Sending a
# checkout's node_modules is the difference between a two-second and a
# two-minute context upload, and sending a host's bundle would let a stale
# `make ui` decide what the image serves — so both build outputs stay out and
# the Node stage's is the only one there is (#11).
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
ui/.svelte-kit/
ui/test-results/
ui/playwright-report/
internal/ui/dist/

# Neither half of the build reads these.
testdata/
specs/
docs/
sdk/
scratch

# The documentation site's build output and the environment of its toolchain
# (spec 050): `COPY . .` would carry both, a virtualenv's worth, into the
# context.
site/
scripts/docs-site/.venv/

# What a working checkout accumulates and an image has no use for.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.bak
.dev.log
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
